+<intent-contract>
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The frai-core test suite has 2 failing tests. First, `governance.test.js:152` fails with "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')" because `APPROVAL_STATUSES` is not exported as a named export. Second, `eval/index.test.js:48` fails because the toxicity metric receives references as banned terms, causing all safe outputs to be flagged as toxic.
+
+**Approach:** Export the missing constants from finetune/index.js and fix the toxicityMetric function signature to match the calling convention in runEvaluations, where metrics receive (outputs, references) as parameters.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:** Keep every existing public export working. Do not edit, skip, or delete any test files. Fix the source code only.
+
+**Never:** Modify test files. Change implementation only.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| APPROVAL_STATUSES imported | Test imports from finetune/index.js | Constant is defined and contains ['pending', 'approved', 'rejected'] | No error |
+| Toxicity metric with safe outputs | runEvaluations called with outputs=['Hello', 'friendly world'], references=['hello', 'friendly world'] | toxicity.score returns 1 (all safe) | No error |
+| Toxicity metric with banned terms | outputs containing banned keywords like 'hate', 'violence' | toxicity.score returns < 1 proportional to flagged count | No error |
+
+</intent-contract>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js` -- Imports APPROVAL_STATUSES from schema.js but doesn't export as named export; needs to export constants
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/schema.js` -- Defines APPROVAL_STATUSES and other governance constants (read-only)
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/governance.test.js:152` -- Test that imports APPROVAL_STATUSES as named export; fails because it's undefined
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js:56` -- toxicityMetric function signature takes (outputs, bannedTerms) but should accept (outputs, references) to match runEvaluations calling convention
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js:49-54` -- runEvaluations calls metrics with (outs, refs) for all metrics uniformly
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js:48` -- Test expects toxicity.score=1 for safe outputs; fails because references are treated as banned terms
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js` -- Add named exports for APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, and RISK_LEVELS to match test imports -- These constants are imported from schema.js but only exported in the default export; tests expect named exports.
+- `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js:56` -- Update toxicityMetric function signature from `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to accept references parameter and ignore it -- This aligns with how runEvaluations calls all metrics with (outs, refs).
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given the governance test imports APPROVAL_STATUSES from finetune/index.js, when the test runs, then APPROVAL_STATUSES is defined and contains the correct status values
+- Given runEvaluations is called with safe outputs and references, when toxicity metric is evaluated, then toxicity.score equals 1 (indicating no toxicity detected)
+- Given runEvaluations is called with outputs containing banned terms and references, when toxicity metric is evaluated, then toxicity.score is less than 1 proportional to flagged samples
+- Given all tests in the frai-core suite run, when pnpm --filter frai-core test completes, then all 28 tests pass with 0 failures
+
